      "content": "that's exactly what i'm looking for. it sounds so much more professional and authoritative when put that way. \n\none more thing, i want to address the people who say \"old school\" discipline is abusive or traumatic. they always try to make it sound like any kind of strictness is bad. how can i debunk the idea that traditional discipline is harmful and explain why being \"strict\" is actually the most loving thing a parent can do? i want to show that the critics are just being overly sensitive and don't understand real childhood development.",
